{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals","id":1385021,"title":"Manual of Exalted Power Eternals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T23:59:57-07:00","id":1385021,"title":"Manual of Exalted Power Eternals","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Today i finally released what has been a 2 year project of a new exalt type for exalted 2.5. Below is a link to the book and I am happy to answer any and all questions on the product.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/311935/Manual-of-Exalted-Power-Eternals?view_as_pub=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...?view_as_pub=1</a></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T00:14:31-07:00","id":1385023,"title":"","content":"Could you give a little summary of the concept and what makes them distinct from other Exalted? I\u2019m definitely interested, but given the price I\u2019d like to know a bit more before I spend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T00:37:43-07:00","id":1385026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385023#post1385023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give a little summary of the concept and what makes them distinct from other Exalted? I\u2019m definitely interested, but given the price I\u2019d like to know a bit more before I spend.</div> </div> </div> </div>spotted this in the &quot;full size preview&quot; for the book :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Eternal Exalted rely upon the spiritual refinement of the four Virtues to power their Charms, making their magic truly unique among the Exalted. They gain power from sacrifice and emotion, and are most mighty when abiding by the tenets of Virtue and their own Motivations. [...] As the Exalts of Soul, the Eternals possess the unique ability to blend the essence of their being with those of other heroes, sharing their ideals, abilities, and even Charms. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T00:40:54-07:00","id":1385027,"title":"","content":"Happily, they are virtue based exalts lost to history during the primordial war and reawakened and freed due to the events of the age of sorrows. They thrive on the interconnection between people and once acted as the mediators of the chosen host, assuring their mental and spiritual health and safety. They excel at turning enemies into friends and introduce a lot of new ways to interact with demons, fair folk, elementals, and ghosts, in some cases changing these entities natures such that they offer whole new play experiences in and of themselves. Their combat style is offensive burster with strong passive defenses but their combat capacity and strategy is highly dependent on the alignment of their virtues, motivation, and intimacies, if their soul aligns with their actions then they can be an unstoppable force of nature but pushed against their own convictions and they can be shattered. They encourage players to engage with the the people around them as the bonds with others empowers them and having friends is their greatest strength. Also has expanded fair folk and ghost creation rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:40:14-07:00","id":1385030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385027#post1385027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happily, they are virtue based exalts lost to history during the primordial war and reawakened and freed due to the events of the age of sorrows. They thrive on the interconnection between people and once acted as the mediators of the chosen host, assuring their mental and spiritual health and safety. They excel at turning enemies into friends and introduce a lot of new ways to interact with demons, fair folk, elementals, and ghosts, in some cases changing these entities natures such that they offer whole new play experiences in and of themselves. Their combat style is offensive burster with strong passive defenses but their combat capacity and strategy is highly dependent on the alignment of their virtues, motivation, and intimacies, if their soul aligns with their actions then they can be an unstoppable force of nature but pushed against their own convictions and they can be shattered. They encourage players to engage with the the people around them as the bonds with others empowers them and having friends is their greatest strength. Also has expanded fair folk and ghost creation rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea about Mediators of the Exalted Host! I knew someone would do Virtue based Exalts for Vault eventually, as that was the most common suggestion in fanmade circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:40:54-07:00","id":1385031,"title":"","content":"Sounds fascinating. Are they the original Soulsteel wielding Exalted that the Sentinel Alchemicals were blueprints for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:56:37-07:00","id":1385036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385031#post1385031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds fascinating. Are they the original Soulsteel wielding Exalted that the Sentinel Alchemicals were blueprints for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, they get a lot of notes on how they interact with Alchemcials, such as the effects of their resonance with the Soulsteel Sentinals, We also include a new caste of Alchemical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:04:57-07:00","id":1385038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385030#post1385030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea about Mediators of the Exalted Host! I knew someone would do Virtue based Exalts for Vault eventually, as that was the most common suggestion in fanmade circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hard part with virtue based exalts is to balance favoring so much of their charmset, we resolved it by dividing their charmset into &quot;Ways&quot; each of which uses 2 virtues each so you can only favor fully 3 ways at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:14:24-07:00","id":1385711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385031#post1385031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds fascinating. Are they the original Soulsteel wielding Exalted that the Sentinel Alchemicals were blueprints for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Kore's cowriter, so I wanted to step in here as well to field a few questions for interested buyers. One thing that hasn't come up yet: this book gives you rules for making TWO kinds of Celestial Exalts, not just one. The first are the chosen of Kore, goddess of the dead, who attune naturally to Soulsteel and can rob others of their powers. The second are the chosen of Wotan, original god of humanity and of life, who naturally attune to Electrum, which is a type of amber distilled from lower souls, and can give their powers to others. They are BOTH Eternal Exalts, as their Incarna were twins, and can with effort learn the Charms of both &quot;Polarities,&quot; as we call them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T08:20:15-07:00","id":1385838,"title":"","content":"This sounds interesting. I was never a big fan of the four Virtues in general, but a lot of the concepts based on them turned out pretty cool (I always liked the Four Arguments of Virtue). I'll check this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:42:44-07:00","id":1385870,"title":"","content":"So here's my initial assessment: this is a good product. The writing is fun and interesting and feels very Exalted. I haven't gotten through all of the Charms and Truths yet, and I'm not the best qualified to assess them for game balance anyway, but nothing I've seen yet looks unreasonable and the writers clearly have a solid grasp of Exalted mechanics.<br /> <br /> The Eternals' version of the Great Curse makes me twitchy, because it seems pretty harsh overall, but I've never been a fan of Great Curse mechanics in general so the problem is probably on my end. I am not sure how to feel about Eternals (and their patrons) having Virtues that go above 5 at high Essence (since it's sort of canon that even the Sun doesn't have Virtues above 5), but I don't think it breaks anything that wasn't already broken. (Essence 6+ was always a mess in 2.5, so I can't imagine this makes it any worse.)<br /> <br /> Also, I am obnoxiously picky about spelling and grammar, and this book hasn't annoyed me even once.<br /> <br /> Overall, this is weird, but it was definitely worth the price and I encourage others to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:11:21-07:00","id":1385875,"title":"","content":"The virtues being able to rise beyond 5 existed with dragon kings for the same reason we gave it to the eternals, for virtue based powers they need to for E6+ effects. Thank you for the review <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:27:57-07:00","id":1385892,"title":"","content":"I do have one question so far: Redemption of the Splintered Soul (p. 117) says: &quot;This Charm has never been successfully used upon a demon of the second circle, and probably lacks the power to free entities so close to their creator\u2019s truth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a missing word or phrase somewhere here? The context of the Charm makes it seem like it <i>should</i> work on second circle demons (IIRC, first circle demons aren't really part of the soul hierarchy at all). By any chance, should the Charm potentially work on second- but not third-circle demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:34:53-07:00","id":1385895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385892#post1385892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have one question so far: Redemption of the Splintered Soul (p. 117) says: &quot;This Charm has never been successfully used upon a demon of the second circle, and probably lacks the power to free entities so close to their creator\u2019s truth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a missing word or phrase somewhere here? The context of the Charm makes it seem like it <i>should</i> work on second circle demons (IIRC, first circle demons aren't really part of the soul hierarchy at all). By any chance, should the Charm potentially work on second- but not third-circle demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that it will work on 2nd circles but you can't start with one.and we wanted to leave weather it would work on 3rd circles up to storyteller discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","user":"korekore","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:10:49-07:00","id":1385908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385895#post1385895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was that it will work on 2nd circles but you can't start with one.and we wanted to leave weather it would work on 3rd circles up to storyteller discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's about what I was thinking. It should probably say something like &quot;...and probably lacks the power to free entities so close to their creator\u2019s truth as demons of the third circle&quot; in that case.<br /> <br /> Also: &quot;Mein of Innocence Evasion&quot; (p. 146) should probably be &quot;Mien.&quot; Still, I'm halfway through the book and that's the first spelling mistake I've seen, so that's a pretty damned good track record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:53:57-07:00","id":1385926,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the catches, I am sure we have a couple like that despite our combing of things that aren't communicating as we wanted. I will say something I am really enjoying about the storytellers vault process is the ability to do updates. We will be taking yours and others commentary and doing updates, when that happens everyone who bought a copy gets an email to redownload it. It is also how we will be adding art assets, as we get funds from the sale to commission them, to replace the free ones from the exalted art packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T18:38:27-07:00","id":1385988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1385908#post1385908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: &quot;Mein of Innocence Evasion&quot; (p. 146) should probably be &quot;Mien.&quot; Still, I'm halfway through the book and that's the first spelling mistake I've seen, so that's a pretty damned good track record.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, that's embarrassing! Yes it's a reference to faces, not noodles, I'll fix that now.<br /> <br /> We did leave a few things in the book strictly up to ST discretion because we recognized that they could be pretty game breaking but might still be worth the chaos for some tables. Totally agree with you about Virtues, honestly. I had the same reaction when Kore pitched the idea, but it resulted in some really solid and unique mechanics for them. One of these days I'll still have to write my Virtue 2.0 hack where players can mix and match any four Virtues to flesh out their character, similar to the common rules hack Scion uses, but this book required a pretty rigorous and stable definition of what a &quot;good guy&quot; is, so we just included a lot of sidebars about how that archetype can be subverted without changing the actual rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:44:54-07:00","id":1389383,"title":"","content":"Hello Everyone and thank you for your support. Today is the last day of the play it forward campaign and thanks to those who have pitched in we have been able to add many new art items and really make the Eternals come to life. We should be adding the cover art we were able to commission from your purchases soon and hope you are all enjoying our work. For those who want an easy reference for their charms or want to get a better feel for Eternals we have added a free download of their unique charm trees. <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/313878/Eternals-Way-Trees</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T17:10:29-07:00","id":1389496,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/311935.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Our cover is up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","user":"korekore","date":".  new cover font 05-21-2020, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T20:50:55-07:00","id":1389556,"title":"","content":"Oh that is damn sweet. Very awesome picture there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:11:37-07:00","id":1396514,"title":"","content":"I did not expect another 2nd Edition supplement!<br /> <br /> Thank you, <b>Korekore</b>!<br /> <br /> I have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1.) Would it be possible for m<span style=\"font-size:12px\">e to get a &quot;I bought/supported Exalted- Eternals&quot; virtual pin to put in my signiture?<br /> <br /> 2.) How much would you suggest to donate for the</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/313878/Eternals-Way-Trees\" target=\"_blank\"> Eternals Way Trees</a> on drivethrurpg?<br /> <br /> What is the next project you are working on?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:54:23-07:00","id":1396531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396514#post1396514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not expect another 2nd Edition supplement!<br /> <br /> Thank you, <b>Korekore</b>!<br /> <br /> I have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1.) Would it be possible for m<span style=\"font-size:12px\">e to get a &quot;I bought/supported Exalted- Eternals&quot; virtual pin to put in my signiture?<br /> <br /> 2.) How much would you suggest to donate for the</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/313878/Eternals-Way-Trees\" target=\"_blank\"> Eternals Way Trees</a> on drivethrurpg?<br /> <br /> What is the next project you are working on?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> 1. I will see what we can do and get back to you on that.<br /> 2. We put it up as a free supplement so people could look at it to reference for their charm purchases and some free advertising to encourage people to buy it. It doesn't have any new material beyond the main book but any money you put towards it will go towards our art budget.<br /> <br /> Next up I am working on a compass of celestial direction to fully flesh out the city of the Yaksha mentioned in Eternals and my co-writer kindledRadial is doing a rewrite of the Sidereals book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:32:49-07:00","id":1396932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396531#post1396531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am ecstatic.<br /> <br /> That cover is <b>gorgeous</b>, BTW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396531#post1396531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I will see what we can do and get back to you on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to show my support &amp; make everyone aware I support <u>you &amp; your crew</u>, <u>2nd Edition</u>, &amp; <u>ST Vault</u>. I am proud of this &amp; I put my $$$ behind my mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396531#post1396531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. We put it up as a free supplement so people could look at it to reference for their charm purchases and some free advertising to encourage people to buy it. It doesn't have any new material beyond the main book but any money you put towards it will go towards our art budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a<span style=\"font-size:14px\">n art budget for future supplements?<br /> <br /> Random Q: Can Drivethrurpg offer a &quot;Print on Demand&quot; option for ST Vault books? I love solid books &amp; PDF's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396531#post1396531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next up I</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396531#post1396531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am working on a compass of celestial direction to fully flesh out the city of the Yaksha mentioned in Eternals and my co-writer kindledRadial is doing a rewrite of the Sidereals book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. LOVE. IT.<br /> <br /> Do you both have a website or similar sites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 06-16-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:44:19-07:00","id":1396933,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the flattery. The art budget is to add more custom assets both for Eternals and to likely reuse in future supplements. We don't have our own websites at the moment but we will see what the future holds. In the meanwhile I am happy to answer any questions you may have on the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:16:18-07:00","id":1396989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1396514#post1396514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What is the next project you are working on?[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>So glad to see someone getting some real enjoyment out of our work!<br /> For those who are curious our next big art asset goal is to pay the cover artist (Tijana Jankovic, to those who want to look up the rest of her amazing work) to color the Caste pictures I drew for the book. Currently they are just lineart, and I'm not being humble when I say that Tijana is five times the artist I am. We're about halfway to our goal for that, and as soon as we can afford it we'll be commissioning her to color those Eternals and make them look truly done. After that, we'll see, but at present 100% of our profits are being funneled into making this book better for those who have bought it or plan to buy it in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 06-16-2020, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:14:19-07:00","id":1397310,"title":"","content":"So, when is it coming for 3rd edition? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:53:49-07:00","id":1397318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1397310#post1397310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when is it coming for 3rd edition? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, I am guessing you read our commentary that we will not be doing this in the page 5 sidebar. That said your are not the first to ask and, while the mechanics would need some major adjustments (hard to have a virtue based exalt with a system that lacks virtues) their fluff and themes slot in just fine to 3rd editions themes and more high magic/low tech feel. The intimacy tiers are also something which I wish 2nd edition had as they would be great at adjusting those tiers and would likely have made up the main push of their social set. So while we won't be writing it if anyone wants to try to adapt it for their table I am happy to advise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T18:05:21-07:00","id":1397867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1397318#post1397318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(hard to have a virtue based exalt with a system that lacks virtues)</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally legit point. My best guess would be that you could model something similar using the mechanics for Intimacies, specifically principles. Charms that require a given number of Virtue-based intimacies at a given intensity as prerequisites... which could open the door to Eternal exalts who have to be very deliberate managing their beliefs and values, because they could actually find themselves cut off from accessing powers they know because they no longer meet the prerequisites to use them (or, as such a condition is something we haven't seen in Third Edition's rule model as yet, you could bake the modality of that powerdown into the charms, so that an Eternal still has access to SOME of that power even if they don't maintain the practice of those 'virtues').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:32:03-07:00","id":1398011,"title":"","content":"Using number of intimacies as minimums for charms might get a bit tricky. When/if 3E gets around to fair folk and dragon kings and I can see the direction for their charm minimums I should be able to work from there. That said the easiest would be to port virtues to 3E as a unique trait statistic to Eternals similar to colleges for sidereals and run things from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:14:48-07:00","id":1398262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1397867#post1397867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally legit point. My best guess would be that you could model something similar using the mechanics for Intimacies, specifically principles. Charms that require a given number of Virtue-based intimacies at a given intensity as prerequisites... which could open the door to Eternal exalts who have to be very deliberate managing their beliefs and values, because they could actually find themselves cut off from accessing powers they know because they no longer meet the prerequisites to use them (or, as such a condition is something we haven't seen in Third Edition's rule model as yet, you could bake the modality of that powerdown into the charms, so that an Eternal still has access to SOME of that power even if they don't maintain the practice of those 'virtues').</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually quite similar to what I had been thinking for a 3rd ed port, but it would be by no means a quick fix. As you mentioned, there will always be situations where none of your Intimacies apply to a given situation, whereas the Virtues are so broadly applicable that its legitimately hard to think of a situation where NONE of them apply. That said, I think 3rd ed could do with a quick and dirty term for the &quot;point value&quot; of sentimentality: you add up all the Intimacies that support the action (1st tiers are one point, second are 2, third are 3), subtract any Intimacies that oppose the action, and what you're left with is your &quot;Emotional Investment Value&quot; or some such. The whole point of Eternals was that they were passion-powered, so whereas 2nd ed models that with Virtues it would be interesting to use Intimacies in 3rd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T19:30:55-07:00","id":1398274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1398262#post1398262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I think 3rd ed could do with a quick and dirty term for the &quot;point value&quot; of sentimentality: you add up all the Intimacies that support the action (1st tiers are one point, second are 2, third are 3), subtract any Intimacies that oppose the action, and what you're left with is your &quot;Emotional Investment Value&quot; or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little more mechanically complex than I'd think would be necessary. I'd lean more towards charm prerequisites that call for 'A Defining compassion-based intimacy', or 'two Temperance-based intimacies' because while that might take more words, and call for the Storyteller being on board, it's quicker to quantify at a glance. <br /> <br /> A similar mechanic might be to have the charms actually auto-upgrade based on the intensity of whichever intimacy they are being used to act upon. Fighting to defend kids? Your magic will work better based on the intensity of the intimacy you have in relation to those kids... like, converted directly into bonus dice. <br /> <br /> You could even build charm mechanics that link specifically to intimacies, ensuring that a given intimacy will never diminish below a certain point, reflecting the fact that the character magically will never NOT care about whichever thing that intimacy applies to. <br /> <br /> Fact is, intimacies are how the 3rd edition models stuff that 1st edition modeled with Virtues, and 2nd edition only really kept them on as a lingering legacy mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:16:49-07:00","id":1398419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1398274#post1398274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a little more mechanically complex than I'd think would be necessary. I'd lean more towards charm prerequisites that call for 'A Defining compassion-based intimacy', or 'two Temperance-based intimacies' because while that might take more words, and call for the Storyteller being on board, it's quicker to quantify at a glance.<br /> <br /> A similar mechanic might be to have the charms actually auto-upgrade based on the intensity of whichever intimacy they are being used to act upon. Fighting to defend kids? Your magic will work better based on the intensity of the intimacy you have in relation to those kids... like, converted directly into bonus dice.<br /> <br /> You could even build charm mechanics that link specifically to intimacies, ensuring that a given intimacy will never diminish below a certain point, reflecting the fact that the character magically will never NOT care about whichever thing that intimacy applies to.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are really good suggestions! And you're right, the reason I discarded the &quot;sum value&quot; Intimacy mechanic idea was that it required a reconsideration of values for every Excellency-enhanced roll. A simpler solution would be to simply have the player pick a few 2nd-tier Intimacies to base their magic off of. In fact, you could allow an unlimited number of Excellencies in that way, each one adding dice to the others up to their 10-die max cap (which would have to be based off of something else, possibly Willpower). Maybe their Castes are still Virtue-based, but that just informs which Intimacy Excellency you take for free at starting: If you are a Mercy Caste then you pick an immutable Intimacy based on helping others, if Courage then it must be an Intimacy that requires conflict to fulfill, etc.<br /> <br /> Only issue would be the Charm prereqs. Intimacies SHOULD be mutable, since players often find that Intimacies they thought should define them at the start of a game need adjustment later, and I'd hate for Eternals to be boxed in to supporting an old and outdated character concept for Charm reasons. In other words, if you base your Charm loadout off of &quot;loving kids&quot; and then you have one and realize that kids are awful, your entire Charmset shouldn't disappear. It might, in all honestly, be easier to only give them Essence prereqs and just have the Charms only work when Intimacies apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 06-23-2020, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T08:23:32-07:00","id":1399291,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing it, but when I'm looking at the Anima Effect powers of the various castes, I don't see any activation costs listed. Can they simply use them at will for free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T09:17:31-07:00","id":1399301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sadric of Ysyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1399291#post1399291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing it, but when I'm looking at the Anima Effect powers of the various castes, I don't see any activation costs listed. Can they simply use them at will for free?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a for benefit one listed generally second but the first and more powerful effect require the expenditure of a virtue channel instead of motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T21:44:56-07:00","id":1399731,"title":"","content":"OK, gotcha, thanks! Another question, more fluff than crunch: I saw a couple of places throughout the book where it refers to the Eternal equivalent of a Solar Perfect Circle as a Square, two pairs of karmic twins, including one of each of the four Castes. I was thinking, though, wouldn't a more &quot;perfect&quot; grouping of Eternal Exalted be an Octagon? Four pairs of karmic twins, including one Bringer and one Keeper of each of the four Castes? (Plus, you know, turn an 8 on its side, you get \u221e... Kinda goes with Eternity) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> That plus the awesomeness of soul-sharing Truths would mean we get to make Sense8 an Exalted story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26206,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","user":"Sadric of Ysyr","date":". 06-29-2020, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:46:25-07:00","id":1399841,"title":"","content":"It was considered, we ended up going with the square since most games won't have 8 players and it would let them distribute better in assignment to solar circles in the age of glory. Two squares working together would have been a auspicious number though I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T13:19:25-07:00","id":1399903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sadric of Ysyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1399731#post1399731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, gotcha, thanks! Another question, more fluff than crunch: I saw a couple of places throughout the book where it refers to the Eternal equivalent of a Solar Perfect Circle as a Square, two pairs of karmic twins, including one of each of the four Castes. I was thinking, though, wouldn't a more &quot;perfect&quot; grouping of Eternal Exalted be an Octagon? Four pairs of karmic twins, including one Bringer and one Keeper of each of the four Castes? (Plus, you know, turn an 8 on its side, you get \u221e... Kinda goes with Eternity) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That plus the awesomeness of soul-sharing Truths would mean we get to make Sense8 an Exalted story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely love where your story is at there! But yeah, the REAL reason we made their traditional grouping a 4 person thing was because we know from our own experience that groups of more than five players quickly become unwieldy, plus its hard to organize that many people every week, and we didn't want to make that like a standard thing.<br /> <br /> The square also left open this theme of Eternals being &quot;support&quot; Exalts, and the expectation that they would travel with other Exalted and use Truths to split their charms which is TERRIFYING in practice. A square of four Eternals all armed with different and broadly-applicable Charms and soul sharing can turn a mere mortal into a celestial powerhouse, nevermind a Solar or Lunar.<br /> <br /> As an addendum to the Caste Anima Banner question, Eternals simply do not have a mote cost to activate their caste anima powers. They have one power that is always on even when they don't flare at all, and one power that is sort of a trump card effect that requires a Virtue channel to power. But no motes are required, and they can use either effect at any level of anima flare, including no flare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T05:17:01-07:00","id":1400281,"title":"","content":"Thanks again! I gotta say these guys are a really great concept, and I'm liking them more and more the more I read. Thanks for all your efforts putting this together!<br /> <br /> I do have another question, this time about Limit. Given that Eternal Charms are Virtue-based, it stands to reason that they would need to develop their Virtues to high ratings in order to access their greater powers. However, if they accrue Limit any time they suppress ANY Virtue rated 3+, aren't they ultimately going to end up as walking Limit capacitors? I realize you created the new mechanic of Limit Release actions to try and compensate for this, but what do you think about perhaps scaling back the accrual of Limit to any time they suppress their Caste or Favored Virtues (which, let's be honest, are pretty much always going to be 3+ right out of the gate)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T09:10:47-07:00","id":1400324,"title":"","content":"Limit was a careful balance. The objective was limit gain on par with abyssal resonance gain since they had the release triggers and placing it on all the virtues achieved that in playtesting. We also leaned towards being too harsh since changing it to be less harsh would be easier for storytellers to implement. The limits themselves are also a bit different being something of a step between a standard celestial limit break and fair folk bedlam so you can potentially play a character in limit break for a few sessions depending on which one you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:45:09-07:00","id":1400346,"title":"","content":"Their Limit Breaks were definitely the most challenging thing to balance for me. Part of what we came up with was an acknowledgement that in our games a lot of times players don't take limit for things they should take limit for because they and the ST flat out forget what their character's Limit Break conditions are. There was also the fear that we had, in same cases, kind of stepped lightly around the canonically accepted fact that Solars are the most powerful Celestial Exalt, so we had to give Eternals an Achilles heel to balance out things like fusion and revival.<br /> <br /> Another factor was that I wanted to change how the Limit Breaks worked so that instead of forcing outrageous behavior for a scene or day you would have to take a &quot;role playing prompt&quot; for an entire session, with relatively mild mechanical drawbacks. The idea was that the Limit Breaks would start to feel more like character flaws than temporary madness. Like if you take the Passion of Fortune, people you travel with just know that you are a spend thrift, and that you can sometimes be cartoonishly miserly about money. Compare that with the Solar Temperance Flaw Overindulgence, where your character does nothing but commit debaucheries all day. So they last longer and build up faster, but they are easier and more enjoyable to play through.<br /> <br /> That said, if your players DO find this sort of Limit Break annoying, then by all means scale back the rules a bit. Only giving Limit when they suppress their Caste/Favored Virtue would be one way, though you could also just let the occasional Limit Break condition slide without a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T19:53:16-07:00","id":1403326,"title":"","content":"If you have been considering picking up the book and haven't yet there is currently a sale going on for not only Eternals but all books on the Storytellers vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T22:28:55-07:00","id":1404707,"title":"","content":"I know this is unlikely to be a question that comes up in practice in a game, but reading the book I'm curious as to the relationship between Kore and Taru-Han.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T22:38:02-07:00","id":1404710,"title":"","content":"Originally would have been a sub god of hers now the order of eternity would be pissed at her and should kore return... Hard to say actually but while she might understand the temptation I would see her being upset..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","user":"korekore","date":".  Thought you said han than not taru han 07-26-2020, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:11:24-07:00","id":1404818,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1166_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1166\" data-vbnamecard=\"1166\">korekore</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1318_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1318\" data-vbnamecard=\"1318\">kindledRadial</a>, is there any chance that there might be a physical printing of the book? I'd be interested, if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:17:43-07:00","id":1404821,"title":"","content":"Sadly storytellers vault has advised that it would be too difficult to do print on demand for any of the fan made products and due to the licence agreement we can't sell physical copies separately. I really wish we could as do many of the authors but we have been told it's a non starter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:25:15-07:00","id":1404823,"title":"","content":"Unfortunate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T21:34:20-07:00","id":1404877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385021-manual-of-exalted-power-eternals?p=1404707#post1404707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is unlikely to be a question that comes up in practice in a game, but reading the book I'm curious as to the relationship between Kore and Taru-Han.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Taru-Han would originally have been a subordinate of Kore but has by now completely forgotten those old obligations, as well as Kore's firm stance on the essential dignity of human souls. Were she to return, she'd be furious, but Kore has always been hard to predict, much like Luna. Hard to say what sort of punishment she would prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T12:35:36-07:00","id":1405397,"title":"","content":"Thanks to MrGone new interactive character sheets are now available <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Exalted/Exalted2ndED4-Page_Eternals_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a></span></span>